  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The concept of sustainability has been around for decades, but its importance has gained significant attention in recent years. One of the main reasons is the growing awareness of climate change and its devastating effects on the environment. Governments, corporations, and individuals are now more than ever acknowledging the need to adopt sustainable practices in their daily lives.\n\nHowever, despite this increased awareness, many people still struggle with understanding what sustainability truly means. Some view it as a luxury only accessible to developed countries, while others see it as an excuse for governments to implement stricter regulations. In reality, sustainability is not just about saving the planet; it's also about creating jobs and stimulating economic growth.\n\nA recent study found that investing in sustainable infrastructure can generate significant returns on investment, with some projects yielding up to 20% annual returns. Moreover, sustainable practices have been shown to improve public health by reducing pollution levels and promoting green spaces.\n\nWhile there is still much work to be done, the shift towards sustainability is undoubtedly underway. As individuals, we must continue to educate ourselves about the importance of sustainability and take action in our daily lives. By doing so, we can contribute to a more environmentally conscious and economically stable future.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main reason for the increased attention on sustainability?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Climate change\", \"Economic growth\", \"Government regulations\", \"Environmental awareness\"],\n      \"answer\": \"B2-C1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"According to the text, what percentage of annual returns can some sustainable infrastructure projects yield?\",\n      \"options\": [\"10%\", \"15%\", \"20%\", \"25%\"],\n      \"answer\": \"C\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"The author's attitude towards sustainability is primarily:\",\n      \"options\": [\"Critical\", \"Neutral\", \"Supportive\", \"Ambivalent\"],\n      \"answer\": \"C\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What can be inferred about sustainable practices from the text?\",\n      \"options\": [\"They only benefit developed countries\", \"They have no impact on public health\", \"They can stimulate economic growth and create jobs\", \"They are only relevant to governments\"],\n      \"answer\": \"C\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"The purpose of the text is primarily to:\",\n      \"options\": [\"Convince readers to adopt sustainable practices\", \"Inform readers about the benefits of sustainability\", \"Entertain readers with a story about climate change\", \"Persuade readers to invest in sustainable infrastructure\"],\n      \"answer\": \"B\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
